
# ---- subject line ------------------------------------------------------
# Write it on the blank first line, as:
#
#   <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
#   type     feat | fix | refactor | perf | style | docs | test | build |
#            ci | chore | revert          (chore is the catch-all)
#   scope    optional; the sub-project or area touched, e.g. include, cmd,
#            tests, py, c, rust, csharp, wasm, benches, fuzzing, scripts,
#            docsgen, ci
#   subject  lowercase, imperative mood, no trailing period, <= 72 columns
#
# ---- body (optional) ---------------------------------------------------
# Wrap at 72 columns. Explain why the change is needed; the diff already
# shows what changed.
#
# ---- footers (optional) ------------------------------------------------
#   Closes #123
#   Assisted-by: <model name> [<version if known>]
#   Generated-by: <model name> [<version if known>]
#
# Use Assisted-by after the human contributor has reviewed, understood, and
# accepted the model-produced content. Generated-by identifies substantially
# model-produced content without that level of human validation; this project
# does not accept such contributions. Use one trailer per participating model.
# Replace the placeholders with the exact model identity provided by the
# environment. Omit an unknown version rather than guessing.
#
# See CONTRIBUTING.md.
#
# ---- full example ------------------------------------------------------
#
#   fix(rust): free strings through C API
#
#   The binding leaked the converted buffer whenever conversion returned an
#   error, because the error path skipped the deallocation helper.
#
#   Closes #399
#
# ---- enable this template ----------------------------------------------
#   git config commit.template .gitmessage
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
